1, E042-E045**: Network connections from MORDORDC to WORKSTATION6 (fe80::5cb9:6d15:e592:60fe) and LDAP queries to 172.18.38.5 and localhost (::1) on port 389. These suggest lateral movement and directory service enumeration.\n\n5. **E050**: BITS service start type changed from \"demand start\" to \"auto start\"\u2014a persistence mechanism.\n\nThe most significant behaviors are the command injection via dsregcmd, command execution through CollectGuestLogs, and the suspicious registry/file manipulation."},{"t":12.86,"agent":"hunter","kind":"tool_result","tool":"set_model_response","result":{"assessment":"An attacker executed commands on the domain controller (MORDORDC) through compromised system components and manipulated registry/file data on WORKSTATION6, while establishing lateral movement and directory service enumeration across the network.","hypotheses":[{"behavior":"svchost.exe launched dsregcmd.exe with template variable arguments $(Arg0) $(Arg1) $(Arg2), causing it to write CloudDomainJoin diagnostics to HKLM registry, indicating command injection or template-based code execution on the domain controller.","event_ids":["E038","E040","X1065","X1068"],"keywords":["dsregcmd","command injection","template variables","CloudDomainJoin","registry modification"]},{"behavior":"CollectGuestLogs.exe spawned cmd.exe and conhost.exe on MORDORDC, enabling arbitrary command execution through an Azure guest agent component.","event_ids":["E046","E047","E048","E049"],"keywords":["CollectGuestLogs","cmd.exe","command execution","process spawning","privilege escalation"]},{"behavior":"backgroundTaskHost.exe wrote suspicious registry values (Cookie:, Visited:) to AppContainer storage and ContentDeliveryManager hives while RuntimeBroker.exe deleted Cortana app icon cache files, suggesting data manipulation or exfiltration staging.","event_ids":["E027","E029","E030","E031","E015"],"keywords":["registry modification","AppContainer","ContentDeliveryManager","file deletion","data st